From: SRNet <121732083+SRNet-lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Exit auth: enforce validate before map/accept; signed
 lease admission

- Call SessionEndpoint::validate in session_post_init before any map/accept
  and in map_session_v4/v6 (upstream parsed auth-type=whitelist but never
  enforced it, so stock exits admitted everyone).
- After open/static-token/whitelist, admit a client holding a signed v2
  exit_lease admission for this exit (.sesh) and that client (.sesh),
  unexpired, Ed25519-signed by SR_EXIT_LEASE_ISSUER_PUBKEY, read from
  SR_EXIT_LEASE_ADMISSIONS. Fail closed; unsigned v1 records refused.
- Unit tests (test_exit_lease_admission) and exit-lease-verify tool.
